course: dictionary
lesson: 13502
title: Immaturity: childish or not yet grown
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Immaturity is a noun. It has two meanings, and the words around it show which one is meant. The root word is mature, which means fully grown or developed, and im- means not, so immaturity is the state of not being fully grown or developed yet.
explain: The first meaning is behaving in a silly or childish way that is not right for your age. «Amir giggled and threw paper at the back of the class, and his teacher said it showed immaturity.» The clues are giggled, threw paper and not right for his age.
explain: The second meaning is not being fully grown or developed yet, as with a young animal, plant or fruit. «The apple was small, hard and sour, a sign of its immaturity.» The clues are small, hard and sour: the apple is not ready yet.
explain: Ask yourself: is a person acting childish, or is a living thing not fully grown? A person usually means the first meaning. A plant, animal or fruit usually means the second. To check, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Immaturity is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «a sign of immaturity», not «an immaturity».
fact: Immaturity means behaving in a silly or childish way that is not right for your age, or not being fully grown or developed yet.
fact: An immature frog is a tadpole, and an immature fruit is unripe.
fact: Adults may point out emotional immaturity when someone sulks or giggles at the wrong time.
fact: Useful phrases: «a sign of immaturity», «emotional immaturity», and «the immaturity of the plant».
exercise: «Mia sulked for an hour because she did not get the game she wanted.» What does this show? | A ripe, sweet fruit | Perfect calm and patience | Her height | *A sign of immaturity, behaving childishly for her age
exercise: «The peach was still green and hard, showing its immaturity.» What does immaturity mean here? | A bright, glowing colour | *Not yet fully grown or ripe, like a young fruit | Being grown up and wise | Very silly and noisy
exercise: Which word means not yet fully grown or developed? | frog | fruit | *immature | tadpole
test: «Oscar threw a tantrum over a board game, and his friends rolled their eyes.» If someone says «Oscar's immaturity showed», what do they mean? | *Childish behaviour that is not right for his age | Being calm and patient | A green, unripe apple | Being a fully grown adult
test: Ruby says, «The unripe pear shows its immaturity.» What does she mean? | Behaviour that is silly for its age | The pear is painted | The pear is very sweet | *The pear is not fully ripe yet
exam: Which is an example of immaturity in the science sense? | A child who sulks when they lose | A grown-up who keeps a calm head | A gleaming, ripe red tomato | *A tadpole, which is an immature frog
